    "result_text": "Full suite passes \u2014 **68 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field on the owner response. The endpoint is served through the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` + MapStruct `OwnerMapper`, so I followed that project pattern rather than adding an OfficeFloor step (the value is a pure derivation of already-loaded owner state, like the sibling `locality`/`membershipLevel` fields):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `ownerSegment` property to the `Owner` schema as an enum of the four allowed values (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`), matching the `contactPreference`/`ageBand` style. This generates `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum`.\n\n2. **`util/OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 derives `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n   - TIER: `PREMIUM` when `MembershipLevel.of(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - AREA: `METRO` when the locality (`CustomerCode.regionOf(owner)`, the same source as the existing `locality` field) is one of NSW/VIC/QLD, else `REGIONAL`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `ownerSegment` via `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum.fromValue(OwnerSegment.of(owner))`.\n\nThe two new `Cp55Tests` cases pass: a Sydney (NSW) owner with an email \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`, and a random-city owner with an email \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`.",
